# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# The game used to be one HTML file, and this file still said so long after it
# was split into css/ and js/. Only the HTML had a cache rule, so browsers kept
# serving stale stylesheets and scripts after a deploy: new markup, old layout,
# and a site that looked unchanged no matter what was uploaded.
#
# Two defences now. These headers stop assets being held indefinitely, and the
# asset URLs in index.html carry a ?v= build tag so an already-cached copy
# cannot be reused at all. Bump the tag in index.html on every release.
# SEARCH ENGINES
#
# The games have moved to paths on thexigames.com, so the noindex that held
# crossword.thexigames.com out of the index is gone — removed in the same
# commit as the move, which is the rule the old note set.
#
# THE RULE still stands for every game in the family:
#   on a subdomain  ->  X-Robots-Tag: noindex must be here
#   on its path     ->  it must NOT be
#
# deploy_check enforces it.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

# no-store, not max-age=0. Both are meant to force a check with the server, but
# must-revalidate leaves room for a browser to serve its copy in edge cases —
# session restore, back/forward, an offline moment — and a stale index.html
# pins a player to an old build permanently, because the versioned asset URLs
# it names are the old ones too. The file is 15KB; fetching it every time costs
# nothing next to shipping someone last week's game.
# Never stored. A player must not be pinned to an old build, and index.html is
# what carries the ?v= tag that busts everything else.
#
# One pair of rules per game. These read /css/* and /js/* before the move,
# which matched nothing once the game went into crossword/ — the rules that
# stop a browser pairing new markup with a month-old stylesheet were silently
# doing nothing at all, and the only sign was a cache header changing from
# no-store to the Pages default. Every game added needs its own three lines.
/
  Cache-Control: no-store

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store

/crossword/
  Cache-Control: no-store

/crossword/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store

/crossword/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/crossword/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# XI Word Search — same three rules as the crossword, one pair per game.
/wordsearch/
  Cache-Control: no-store

/wordsearch/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store

/wordsearch/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/wordsearch/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The shared token layer. Immutable is safe because every reference carries a
# ?v= tag and the wordsearch gate asserts the version marker in the file.
/shared/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
